    <string name="break_eye_title">20-20-20 Eye Rest</string>
    <string name="break_eye_body">Every 20 minutes, look at something at least 20 feet (6 metres) away for 20 seconds. Blink intentionally 10 times. Your near-point muscles need the rest.</string>
    <string name="break_hydration_title">Hydration</string>
    <string name="break_hydration_body">A 250 ml glass of water every hour of studying. Carry a bottle to your desk. Add lemon or cucumber if plain water is boring.</string>
    <string name="break_walk_title">Walk + Fresh Air</string>
    <string name="break_walk_body">A 5-minute walk resets attention better than scrolling. Open a window or step outside; 20 deep breaths of outdoor air.</string>
    <string name="break_snack_body">Healthy snacks: a handful of nuts, a banana, yogurt, dark chocolate square, roasted chickpeas. Avoid sugary drinks — the crash will hurt your next session.</string>
